ter support airplay and if your  friend comes over with an android device  he is out of luck not only can echoes  work as a bluetooth speaker so anybody  can connect to it directly  and they can stream to it and they'll  still work if your network is down  but they can also connect to other  bluetooth devices and directly stream to  them  i have a massive fluent speaker that is  insanely  loud which supports bluetooth so with  just my voice i can connect to it and i  can use alexa to stream  and get incredible sound and if you have  speakers that don't support bluetooth  all echoes have three and a half  millimeter outputs  so you can turn your dumb speaker into a  smart one none of this is possible  on the homepod it works best with apple  apps from apple  devices and with music that can only  play on it  and only if your wi-fi is working the  whole pod might be  apple's most locked down device and  anything that connects to it has to be  approved and controlled by apple  which means that there could be a lot  less home kit devices that are out there  and a lot of those are gonna be more  expensive as well now let's circle back  and finish up with audio quality when  listening to music which is probably  what most people spend  most of their time doing with their  smart speakers i'm almost certain that  the mini will sound better than the echo  dots  which share the same 1.6 inch speaker  but that's to be expected at 50 dollars  for the new one  and a crazy 19 right now for the third  gen  these don't sound fantastic but they're  still very usable at medium volumes  and if you buy it for that price which  by the way there's links in the video  description  i don't think anybody's gonna complain  my question is  how it will compare to the new standard  echo that comes in at the same  99 this thing is slightly larger but  features  three speakers instead of one a three  inch woofer and two tweeters that are  about 20 millimeter  my question is how it will compare to 